<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">International Force East Timor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1999–2000</span> · Also known as INTERFET</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The International Force <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a> (INTERFET) was a multinational peacekeeping force led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and authorised by the UN Security Council in September 1999. It deployed after pro-Indonesian militias devastated East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> following its vote for independence, restored security and oversaw the departure of Indonesian forces. In February 2000 it handed over to the UN Transitional Administration in East Timor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/international-force-east-timor.jpg" alt="International Force East Timor" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unbekannt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INTERFET_Logo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
